// The `std` package root. A `lib.vl` is integrated with its directory's module,
// so anything re-exported here would be reachable by the SHORT name `std::x`.
//
// Nothing is. Every entry that used to sit here — `print`, `panic`, `assert`,
// `Default`, `str` and the eleven numerics — existed for one reason: to let a
// caller write `std::print` instead of `std::io::print`. That is import
// brevity, and the prelude serves it properly now (`prelude.md` §10.2), so the
// aliases are gone and each name is spelled at its real home.
//
// The prelude modules are `prelude.vl` (the base set) and `web.vl` (the web
// set). They are ordinary modules; std itself declares `prelude = false` and
// compiles under neither.
